id: pm-si2uur
title: "GH-728: preserve live harness authorship across initialized multi-agent workspaces"
description: "pm init persists the initializing harness as author_default, so later agents inherit a frozen effective author even though structured harness/model observation is current. Stop initialization from freezing an automatically detected harness identity while preserving explicitly configured human/operator defaults and backward-compatible workspace behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ux,"area:sdk",author,identity,multi-agent,provenance
created_at: "2026-07-26T06:25:19.908Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T08:29:30.361Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T07:24:55.763Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Fresh pm init does not persist an automatically detected harness as a static author_default; Mutations by different harnesses in one initialized workspace record the acting harness as effective author without PM_AUTHOR; Explicit operator-configured author_default remains authoritative; SDK and CLI initialization paths share one contract; Isolated multi-harness acceptance verifies history author, harness, and model fields"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Initialized workspaces no longer persist auto-detected harness identity as a static default author.
expected_result: Each harness invocation is attributed to the current harness unless the operator explicitly overrides author.
actual_result: "One fresh installed workspace records harness:codex and harness:claude-code on successive invocations without PM_AUTHOR."
